 "notes": [
  "On 1h, a long after a bullish engulfing gave 14,579 entries in 1,987 separate moves. After 20 candles they were 0% ahead of random entries, with a luck band from -0.06% to 0.05%. A short after a bearish engulfing fired about as often and came out 0.02% ahead, inside a band of -0.05% to 0.05%.",
  "Moving up a timeframe does not change the answer. On 4h the bullish pattern gave 3,652 entries and ended -0.04% against a band of -0.24% to 0.21%. On daily it ended -0.01%, inside a band of -1.97% to 1.54%.",
  "A short after a daily bearish engulfing came closest, 0.71% better than random after 20 days. The luck band runs to 1.57%, so that is chance. Read the other way, as a long after the same candle, it is 0.71% worse, which is also inside its band. On BTC and ETH alone the daily pattern gave 24 and 26 moves, too few to judge.",
  "The default setting goes long on either pattern, so it also buys right after a bearish candle. It enters about twice as often as the bullish pattern alone, but on 1h its 29,311 entries collapse into only 421 separate moves, because the patterns follow each other closely. It ended -0.01% against a band of -0.03% to 0.03%.",
  "No single coin breaks out either. On 1h, SOL shorts after a bearish engulfing came out 0.09% ahead, just under the band's top at 0.10%. On 4h, BTC shorts after the same candle came out -0.15%, inside a band of -0.26% to 0.21%.",
  "For a bot, the engulfing pattern does not time entries on these pairs by itself, so the take profit and DCA orders carry each deal. If you keep it, use the bullish pattern as one filter beside a trend or level condition, and backtest with and without it to see if your deals change. The default either-pattern setting adds the bearish candles too, so for a long bot you can leave it out and lose nothing measurable."
